From c9dd37e04dcb122bbad864b3b23d5db54760f9a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:09:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Round 2 fixes: drag region, samurai offset, Holy recolor,
 daylight default

- Fixed the modern-style pill radius clipping quest card text: it was
  applying the small-chip 999px pill to whole cards, not just chips/tags
  (app.css).
- Fixed drag-to-move for real this time: the sprite button itself was still
  force-set to no-drag even when unlocked, so there was nothing to actually
  grab. It's now part of the drag region; Chromium still treats a
  no-movement mousedown/up as a click, so opening the menu still works
  (app.css).
- Samurai offset increased and now applies only to the idle pose -- the
  crop box is shared across all 10 animations (deliberately, so switching
  animations doesn't resize/re-anchor the sprite), and idle sits in the
  upper-left of a box sized for wider action poses (HeroSprite.tsx).
- Rewrote the Holy skin's recolor theme: was desaturating to 45% and
  routing half the pixels to a cool blue secondary hue -- now both hues
  stay in the warm gold/ivory family with saturation and lightness both
  raised (tools/import_characters.py). Regenerate the art to see it:
  python3 tools/import_characters.py --src <packs> --out public/heroes
- Daylight is now the default theme (settings.ts).
- Quest board cards and Lore entries now use the same condensed
  summary-row + click-to-expand pattern as hero cards, instead of the
  quest popout modal from the last patch (QuestPanel.tsx, LorePanel.tsx).
- Quest result modal no longer says 'Good work' on a failed quest -- the
  button reads 'Understood' instead (QuestResultModal.tsx).
- Guild Hall facility upgrades were the one purchase path missing the
  'purchase' sound cue every other buy action has (engine.ts). Also wired
  facilities into the same max-flash treatment as upgrades/vendors, and
  extracted that into a shared src/ui/maxFlash.tsx instead of duplicating
  it (GuildPanel.tsx, UpgradesPanel.tsx).
- The 9-class hero roster genuinely can fit in the max slot count (1 base +
  5 Tavern + 4 Extra Banner = 10), but Extra Banner is a Prestige/renown
  perk, not a regular upgrade -- it requires retiring a level-30+ hero
  first. Recruit cards and the blocked-banner now say so explicitly
  instead of silently disabling with a misleading 'Recruit' label
  (HeroesPanel.tsx).
- Reworked the Crow's Warning and Proving the Bastion chain intros: the
  former now names 'the cure' explicitly so the latter's callback to it
  isn't ambiguous, and both read less awkwardly (quests.ts).
